    "name": "Laravel CRUD API",
    "description": "## Laravel CRUD API\n\nThis collection covers a RESTful CRUD API built with **Laravel**, organized around three core resources: **Customer**, **Item**, and **Order**.\n\nEach resource folder exposes the same consistent set of five operations:\n\n| Operation | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| **CREATE** | Add a new record |\n| **GET ALL** | Retrieve all records for the resource |\n| **SEARCH** | Query or filter records by specific criteria |\n| **UPDATE** | Modify an existing record |\n| **DELETE** | Permanently remove a record |\n\n### Resources\n\n- **Customer** – Manage customer profiles and their associated data.\n- **Item** – Handle catalog items available within the system.\n- **Order** – Create and manage orders linking customers to items.\n\n### Usage\n\nUse this collection to develop, test, and validate the backend logic for a Laravel application. All endpoints follow a uniform structure, making it easy to extend the API or integrate it with a front-end interface or third-party service.",
